'''Zydus Lifesciences Limited''', formerly known as '''Cadila Healthcare Limited''',<ref>{{cite news |last1=Umarji |first1=Vinay |title=Cadila Healthcare changes name to Zydus Lifesciences Limited |url=https://www.business-standard.com/article/companies/cadila-healthcare-changes-name-to-zydus-lifesciences-limited-122022401005_1.html |access-date=17 March 2022 |work=Business Standard India |date=24 February 2022}}</ref> is an Indian multinational [[pharmaceutical]] company headquartered in [[Ahmedabad]]. Primarily engaged in the manufacturing of [[generic drugs]],<ref name="The Hindu Business Line">{{Cite news|url=http://www.thehindubusinessline.com/companies/announcements/others/zydus-launches-sovihep-the-breakthrough-therapy-for-hepatitis-c-in-alliance-with-gilead-sciences/article7003039.ece|title=Zydus launches SoviHep - the breakthrough therapy for Hepatitis C in alliance with Gilead Sciences|date=2015-03-17|work=The Hindu Business Line|access-date=2017-12-29|language=en}}</ref><ref name="mapsofindia">{{cite web|date=21 June 2011|title=A Complete Overview on Cadila Healthcare, a growing and popular company in India.|url=http://business.mapsofindia.com/sectors/manufacturing/cadila-healthcare.html|access-date=2009-02-04|website=business.mapsofindia.com}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Cadila Healthcare Profit and Loss Reports – The Economic Times|url=https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/cadila-healthcare-ltd/profitandlose/companyid-3778.cms|access-date=2020-06-15|website=economictimes.indiatimes.com}}</ref> the company ranked 100th in the [[Fortune India 500|''Fortune'' India 500]] list in 2020.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Cadila Healthcare – Fortune 500 List 2020 – Fortune India|url=https://www.fortuneindia.com/fortune-500/company-list/cadila-healthcare?year=2020|access-date=2021-01-12|website=fortuneindia.com|language=en}}</ref>

== History ==
Cadila was founded in 1952 by [[Ramanbhai Patel]] (1925–2001), formerly a lecturer in the L.M. College of Pharmacy, and his business partner [[Indravadan Modi]].<ref>{{cite news |title=India's Richest 2019: Cadila's Patels' Quest For The Magic Pill |url=https://www.forbesindia.com/article/india-rich-list-2019/india039s-richest-2019-cadila039s-patels039-quest-for-the-magic-pill/56171/1 |access-date=2 October 2023 |work=Forbes India |language=en}}</ref>

In 1995, the Patel and Modi families split; the Modi family's share was moved into a new company called [[Cadila Pharmaceuticals]], and Cadila Healthcare became the Patel family's holding company. Cadila Healthcare had its [[initial public offering]] in February 2000 and listed on the [[Bombay Stock Exchange|BSE]].<ref>{{cite news |title=Cadila shares close IPO price after 3 years |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/business/india-business/cadila-shares-close-ipo-price-after-3-years/articleshow/101727.cms |access-date=2 October 2023 |work=The Times of India |date=29 July 2003}}</ref>

In 2003, the company [[Mergers and acquisitions|merged]] another Indian pharmaceutical company called German Remedies into itself.<ref>{{cite news |title=German Remedies to be merged with Cadilla |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/business/india-business/german-remedies-to-be-merged-with-cadilla/articleshow/122464.cms |access-date=2 October 2023 |work=The Times of India |date=9 August 2003}}</ref> On 25 June 2007, the company acquired Química e Farmacêutica Nikkho do Brasil Ltda (Nikkho) as part of Zydus Healthcare Brasil Ltda.<ref>[https://www.bloomberg.com/research/stocks/private/snapshot.asp?privcapId=35196980 Company Overview of Química e Farmacêutica Nikkho do Brasil Ltda] ''Bloomberg''</ref>

In 2014, Cadila Healthcare launched the world's first ''[[adalimumab biosimilar]]'' under the brand name Exemptia at one-fifth the originator's price.<ref>[https://web.archive.org/web/20150328064218/http://articles.economictimes.indiatimes.com/2014-12-09/news/56879703_1_rheumatoid-arthritis-first-biosimilar-humira Zydus Cadila launches biosimilar of AbbVie's Humira in India] ''The Economic Times'' 9 December 2014</ref>
Zydus Cadila Healthcare has also launched its first research based drug molecule [[Saroglitazar]] in the treatment of Diabetic Dyslipidemia under brand name "Lipaglyn". SoviHep is the first [[sofosbuvir]] brand launched in India by Zydus in the year 2015.<ref name="The Hindu Business Line"/>

In 2019, injectable [[ketorolac]] tromethamine manufactured by Zydus (Cadila Healthcare) was recalled due to microbial growth.<ref>{{cite news |title=Sagent Pharmaceuticals Issues Voluntary Nationwide Recall of Ketorolac Tromethamine Injection, USP, 60mg/2mL (30mg per mL) Due to Lack of Sterility Assurance |url=https://www.fda.gov/safety/recalls-market-withdrawals-safety-alerts/sagent-pharmaceuticals-issues-voluntary-nationwide-recall-ketorolac-tromethamine-injection-usp |access-date=2 October 2023 |work=FDA |date=29 September 2020 |language=en}}</ref>

In 2020, Zydus Cadila's drug Desidustat received approval by the [[Food and Drug Administration|USFDA]] to initiate clinical trials on [[cancer]] patients.<ref>[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/zydus-cadila-gets-usfda-nod-for-drug-trials-to-treat-chemotherapy-induced-anemia/articleshow/77121315.cms Zydus Cadila Desidustat Gets USFDA Nod To Initiate Clinical Trials On Cancer Patients] ''The Times Of India'' 23 July 2020</ref>

In 2022, Cadila Healthcare Ltd was renamed as Zydus Lifesciences Ltd.<ref>{{cite news |title=Cadila Healthcare changes name to Zydus Lifesciences Limited |url=https://www.business-standard.com/article/companies/cadila-healthcare-changes-name-to-zydus-lifesciences-limited-122022401005_1.html |access-date=2 October 2023 |work=Business Standard}}</ref>

In October 2024, USFDA Approval for Prostate Cancer Drug: Zydus Lifesciences received USFDA approval to manufacture [[enzalutamide]] tablets, which are used for treating [[prostate cancer]]. This drug, an androgen receptor inhibitor, is designed for patients with castration-resistant and metastatic castration-sensitive prostate cancer. The product will be manufactured at Zydus' facility in Ahmedabad. This approval is part of the company's broader efforts to expand its portfolio of cancer treatments in the U.S. market.

In 2025, Zydus acquired the CDMO business of [[Agenus]] including their two biologics manufacturing sites in Emeryville and Berkeley. In addition, they would partner with Agenus to commercialize their molecules in India.<ref>{{cite news |title=Agenus signs agreements for botensilimab and balstilimab |url=https://www.pharmaceutical-technology.com/news/agenus-agreements-botensilimab-balstilimab/?cf-view |work=Pharmaceutical Technology |date=4 June 2025}}</ref>

